From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:18:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] mb/dell/optiplex_3050: Match Dell's DDI E lanes and
 root port settings

Dell's VBT lists a DisplayPort output on DDI E, probably the optional
video port module. coreboot gives all four DDI A lanes to DDI A, so
Linux finds DDI E with no lanes and warns with a stack trace:

  i915 0000:00:02.0: [drm] Not enough lanes (0) for DP on [ENCODER:131:DDI E/PHY E]

Split the lanes between DDI A and DDI E. DDI A drives an internal eDP
panel, which this desktop doesn't have; the HDMI and DP ports are on
DDI B and C and don't change.

Dell's firmware also enables LTR and Advanced Error Reporting on all
three root ports it uses (RP5 for the Realtek LAN, RP8 for the M.2 WLAN
slot and RP21 for the M.2 SSD); the port only enables them on RP21.
Without LTR on its root port, a device can't report its latency
tolerance: Linux enables LTR on a device only when the port above it
supports it, and the PMC then can't let the package into deeper C
states while the link is idle. Without AER, the OS gets no PCIe error
reports from the two slots. Enable both on RP5 and RP8.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/Kconfig                    | 1 +
 .../sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb    | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/Kconfig b/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/Kconfig
index 25afbeb2e6..ea386f420d 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/Kconfig
+++ b/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/Kconfig
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ config BOARD_DELL_SKLKBL_DESKTOPS_COMMON
 config BOARD_DELL_OPTIPLEX_3050
 	bool
 	select BOARD_DELL_SKLKBL_DESKTOPS_COMMON
+	select SOC_INTEL_GFX_ENABLE_DDI_E_BIFURCATION
 	select MAINBOARD_HAS_TPM2
 	select MEMORY_MAPPED_TPM
 
diff --git a/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb b/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb
index c762c4fe3f..3761b4ffc6 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb
@@ -31,12 +31,16 @@ chip soc/intel/skylake
 		device ref pcie_rp5 on
 			register "PcieRpClkReqSupport[4]"		= "false"
 			register "PcieRpHotPlug[4]"			= "0"
+			register "PcieRpAdvancedErrorReporting[4]"	= "1"
+			register "PcieRpLtrEnable[4]"			= "true"
 		end
 
 		# M.2 WiFi
 		device ref pcie_rp8 on
 			register "PcieRpClkReqSupport[7]"		= "false"
 			register "PcieRpHotPlug[7]"			= "0"
+			register "PcieRpAdvancedErrorReporting[7]"	= "1"
+			register "PcieRpLtrEnable[7]"			= "true"
 		end
 
 		# M.2 SSD
